Source: droidloom
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Project SunUEFI <slwyts@tuta.io>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/denialwm/droidloom

Package: droidloom-runtime
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 droidloom-image (= ${binary:Version}),
 systemd (>= 254), dbus-user-session, pkexec, polkitd,
 util-linux, mount, e2fsprogs, iproute2, nftables, iptables,
 adb, pipewire, libvulkan1, tar, zstd
Recommends: wireplumber, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Suggests: rsync
Description: Android applications in native Wayland windows
 Runs Android applications using Linux namespaces and presents each
 application in its own Wayland window. Starts on request.

Package: droidloom-image
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, droidloom-base (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Android vendor and guest components for Droidloom
 Contains the Android vendor partition, guest programs and compatibility
 files. Per-user data is created separately.

Package: droidloom-base
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Android system partitions for Droidloom
 Contains read-only Android system, system_ext and product partitions.
 These images are separate from the device's Android installation.
